#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""error-classes: the error-v1 vocabulary as built (ops/bin/_errors.py) and where it lands.

  history    every `error:` stop in a fixed extract of the ledger (historical-stops.json: 131 distinct
             stops, 7,577 rows, 2026-11-09) classifies to a class other than unclassified; every other
             stop to none, except interrupted and aborted; the per-class row counts are pinned
  shape      every object is {class, code, source, retryable, detail}, detail <= 512 bytes
  calls      tool events: a pre_tool veto, a sandbox exit 101, a kill (timeout or external), a kill by
             the run's own deadline, a plain non-zero exit; a successful call counts nothing
  sandbox    sandbox_denied over cs-sandbox reports (finalize-run groups them per tool): a denial text plus a
             path the effective policy withholds, or a narrowing the failure names; each limit has a control
  readers    row_error classifies a version 1 row on read and returns a version 2 row's own object;
             _void's CONFIG_VOID and repeated_failure answer the same for a v1 row and its v2 twin
  dispatch   tick: an orphaned running job closes with class node_restart; a launcher refusal
             (env_policy) closes with class node_config, code env_policy; stop strings unchanged
Isolated estates only; lab/ledger is never read or written.
"""
